{
  "title": "Duas at Daybreak and Sunset",
  "data": "Surahs & Dhikr before Sunrise\nBefore sunrise, recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116), [Surah al-Qadr](A101) and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) 11 times each.\nIn the first hour of the morning, before sunrise, recite:\nاَللهُ اَكْبَرُ اَللهُ اَكْبَرُ كَبِيْرًا\nALLAAHU AKBARU ALLAAHU AKBARU KABEERAA\nAllah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, greatly;\nوَسُبْحَانَ اللهِ بُكْرَةً وَاَصِيْلًا\nWA SUBHAANALLAAHI BUKRATAN WA ASEELAA\nand glory be to Allah, morning and evening;\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ كَثِيْرًا\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEENA KATHEERAA\nand abundant praise be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.\nلَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهٖ\nLAA SHAREEKA LAHOO WA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nHe has no partner. And may Allah bless Muhammad and his Household.",
  "tabs": [
    "Tahlil ×10\nBefore sunrise and before sunset, recite 10 times every day:\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nThere is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner.\nلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ\nLAHUL MULKU WA LAHUL HAMD\nTo Him is the kingdom and to Him is all praise.\nيُحْيِيْ وَيُمِيْتُ\nYUHYEE WA YUMEET\nHe gives life and causes to die,\nوَهُوَ حَيٌّ لَا يَمُوْتُ بِيَدِهِ الْخَيْرُ\nWA HUWA HAYYUN LAA YAMOOTU BIYADIHIL KHAYR\nwhile He is ever-living and never dies. In His hand is the good,\nوَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nWA HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nand He has power over all things.\nSome narrations read:\nيُحْيِيْ وَيُمِيْتُ وَيُمِيْتُ وَيُحْيِيْ\nYUHYEE WA YUMEETU WA YUMEETU WA YUHYEE\nHe gives life and causes to die and causes to die and gives life,\nSome narrations leave out this phrase:\nوَهُوَ حَيٌّ لَا يَمُوْتُ بِيَدِهِ الْخَيْرُ\nWA HUWA HAYYUN LAA YAMOOTU BIYADIHIL KHAYR\nwhile He is ever-living and never dies. In His hand is the good,\nAny of these forms is acceptable, though the fullest form is best. If you miss it, make it up later.",
    "Takbir ×100 & Tasbih\nBefore sunrise and before sunset, say Allahu Akbar 100 times.\nRecite 10 times or more:\nسُبْحَانَ اللهِ وَبِحَمْدِهٖ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI WA BIHAMDIH\nGlory be to Allah, and praise be to Him.\nRecite once in the morning and once in the evening:\nسُبْحَانَ اللهِ وَبِحَمْدِہٖ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI WA BIHAMDIHEE SUBHAANALLAAHIL A'ZEEM\nGlory be to Allah, and praise be to Him; glory be to Allah, the Great.",
    "Tasbihat al-Arba’a ×10\nEvery morning and evening, recite 10 times:\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَاللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI WAL HAMDU LILLAAHI WA LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WALLAAHU AKBAR\nAll glory be to Allah, all praise be to Allah, there is no god save Allah, and Allah is the Greatest.",
    "Verses of Glorification ×3\nIn the evening and in the morning, recite these verses of [Surah al-Rum](A34) 3 times:\nفَسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ حِيْنَ تُمْسُوْنَ وَحِيْنَ تُصْبِحُوْنَ\nFASUBHAANALLAAHI HEENA TUMSOONA WA HEENA TUSBIHOON\nSo glorify Allah when you enter evening and when you rise at dawn.\nوَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ فِىْ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَعَشِيًّا وَّحِيْنَ تُظْهِرُوْنَ\nWA LAHUL HAMDU FIS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDI WA A'SHIYYAW WA HEENA TUZHIROON\nTo Him belongs all praise in the heavens and the earth, at nightfall and when you enter noontime.",
    "La Hawla & Relief from Poverty\nEvery morning and evening, recite 3 times:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful.\nلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nLAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nThere is no power and no strength except with Allah, the All-high, the All-great.\nEvery morning and evening, recite [Dua for Relief from Poverty & Ailments](E54).",
    "Isti’adha ×10\nBefore sunrise and before sunset, recite 10 times:\nاَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ السَّمِيْعِ الْعَلِيْمِ مِنْ هَمَزَاتِ الشَّيَاطِيْنِ\nA'OODHU BILLAAHIS SAMEE'IL A'LEEMI MIN HAMAZAATISH SHAYAATEEN\nI seek the protection of Allah, the All-hearing and All-knowing, against the evil suggestions of the devils,\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ اَنْ يَحْضُرُوْنِ\nWA A'OODHU BILLAAHI AN YAHDUROON\nand I seek Allah’s protection lest they be present with me.\nاِنَّ اللهَ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nINNALLAAHA HUWAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEM\nVerily, Allah is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.\nSome narrations have, in place of the second phrase:\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ رَبِّ اَنْ يَّحْضُرُوْنِ\nWA A'OODHU BIKA RABBI AY YAHDUROON\nand I seek Your protection, my Lord, from their presence near me.\nOther narrations give it as:\nاَسْتَعِيْذُ بِاللهِ السَّمِيْعِ الْعَلِيْمِ مِنْ هَمَزَاتِ الشَّيَاطِيْنِ\nASTA'EEDHU BILLAAHIS SAMEE'IL A'LEEMI MIN HAMAZAATISH SHAYAATEEN\nI seek refuge with Allah, the All-hearing, the All-knowing, against the evil suggestions of the devils,\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ اَنْ يَحْضُرُوْنِ\nWA A'OODHU BILLAAHI AN YAHDUROON\nand I seek Allah’s protection lest they be present with me.\nاِنَّ اللهَ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nINNALLAAHA HUWAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEM\nVerily, Allah is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.",
    "Dua Muqallib al-Qulub ×3\nRecite 3 times every morning and 3 times every evening:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مُقَلِّبَ الْقُلُوْبِ وَالْاَبْصَارِ\nALLAAHUMMA MUQALLIBAL QULOOBI WAL ABSAAR\nO Allah Who causes the changes of hearts and sights,\nثَبِّتْ قَلْبِيْ عَلٰى دِيْنِكَ\nTHABBIT QALBEE A'LAA DEENIK\n(please) make firm my heart on the course of Your religion,\nوَلَا تُزِغْ قَلْبِيْ بَعْدَ اِذْ هَدَيْتَنِيْ\nWA LAA TUZIGH QALBEE BA'DA IDH HADAYTANEE\ncause not my heart to stray off after You have guided me,\nوَهَبْ لِي مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ رَحْمَةً اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ\nWA HAB LEE MIL LADUNKA RAHMATAN INNAKA ANTAL WAHHAAB\nand bestow upon me mercy from Your Presence. Surely, You are the All-bestower.\nوَاَجِرْنِي مِنَ النَّارِ بِرَحْمَتِكَ\nWA AJIRNEE MINAN NAARI BIRAHMATIK\nAnd save me from Hellfire out of Your mercy.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ امْدُدْ لِي فِي عُمْرِيْ\nALLAAHUMMAM DUD LEE FEE U'MREE\nO Allah, (please) extend my lifetime,\nوَاَوْسِعْ عَلَيَّ فِي رِزْقِيْ\nWA AWSI' A'LAYYA FEE RIZQEE\nexpand my sustenance,\nوَانْشُرْ عَلَىَّ مِنْ رَّحْمَتِكَ\nWANSHUR A'LAYYA MIR RAHMATIK\ncover me with Your mercy,\nوَاِنْ كُنْتُ عِنْدَكَ فِيْ اُمِّ الْكِتَابِ شَقِيًّا\nWA IN KUNTU I'NDAKA FEE UMMIL KITAABI SHAQIYYAA\nand if I am listed in the Mother of the Book with the unhappy ones,\nفَاجْعَلْنِيْ سَعِيْدًا\nFAJ'ALNEE SA'EEDAA\nplease include me with the happy ones,\nفَاِنَّكَ تَمْحُوْ مَا تَشَاۤءُ وَتُثْبِتُ وَعِنْدَكَ اُمُّ الْكِتَابِ\nFA-INNAKA TAMHOO MAA TASHAA'U WA TUTHBITU WA I'NDAKA UMMUL KITAAB\nfor, surely, You efface what You will, and establish what You will, and with You is the Mother of the Book.",
    "Morning Praise\nBegin the day by praising Allah for these four blessings:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ عَرَّفَنِىْ نَفْسَهٗ وَلَمْ يَتْرُكْنِىْ عَمْيَانَ الْقَلْبِ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE A'RRAFANEE NAFSAHOO WA LAM YATRUKNEE A'MYAANAL QALB\nAll praise be to Allah Who has made Himself known to me and has not left me blind of heart.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَنِىْ مِنْ اُمَّةِ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE JA'ALANEE MIN UMMATI MUHAMMADIN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nAll praise be to Allah Who has made me one of the nation of Muhammad, may Allah bless him and his Household.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ رِزْقِىْ فِىْ يَدَيْهِ وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ رِزْقِىْ فِىْ اَيْدِى النَّاسِ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE JA'ALA RIZQEE FEE YADAYHI WA LAM YAJ'AL RIZQEE FEE AYDIN NAAS\nAll praise be to Allah Who has placed my sustenance in His own hands and has not placed my sustenance in the hands of people.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ سَتَرَ ذُنُوْبِىْ وَعُيُوْبِىْ وَلَمْ يَفْضَحْنِىْ بَيْنَ الْخَلَائِقِ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE SATARA DHUNOOBEE WA U'YOOBEE WA LAM YAFDAHNEE BAYNAL KHALAA'IQ\nAll praise be to Allah Who has covered my sins and my faults and has not disgraced me among the creatures.\nIn the morning, recite 3 times:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nAll praise be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ حَمْدًا كَثِيْرًا طَيِّبًا مُبَارَكًا فِيْهِ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHI HAMDAN KATHEERAN TAYYIBAN MUBAARAKAN FEEH\nAll praise be to Allah, with praise abundant, goodly and blessed.",
    "Dua Asbahtu Billahi Mu’minan\nIn the morning, recite:\nاَصْبَحْتُ بِاللهِ مُؤْمِنًا عَلٰى دِيْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَسُنَّتِهٖ\nASBAHTU BILLAAHI MU'MINAN A'LAA DEENI MUHAMMADIN WA SUNNATIH\nI have entered the morning believing in Allah, upon the religion of Muhammad and his Sunnah,\nوَدِيْنِ عَلِيٍّ وَسُنَّتِهٖ وَدِيْنِ الْاَوْصِيَاۤءِ وَسُنَّتِهِمْ\nWA DEENI A'LIYYIN WA SUNNATIHEE WA DEENIL AWSIYAA'I WA SUNNATIHIM\nthe religion of Ali and his Sunnah, and the religion of the Successors and their Sunnah.\nاٰمَنْتُ بِسِرِّهِمْ وَعَلَانِيَتِهِمْ وَشَاهِدِهِمْ وَغَاۤئِبِهِمْ\nAAMANTU BISIRRIHIM WA A'LAANIYATIHIM WA SHAAHIDIHIM WA GHAA'IBIHIM\nI believe in their secret and their open, in those of them who are present and those who are absent.\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِمَّا اسْتَعَاذَ مِنْهُ رَسُوْلُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nWA A'OODHU BILLAAHI MIMMAS TA'AADHA MINHU RASOOLULLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nI seek refuge with Allah from that from which the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and his Household, sought refuge,\nوَعَلِيٌّ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ وَالْاَوْصِيَاۤءُ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ\nWA A'LIYYUN A'LAYHIS SALAAMU WAL AWSIYAA'U A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nand Ali, peace be upon him, and the Successors, peace be upon them.\nوَاَرْغَبُ اِلَى اللهِ فِيْمَا رَغِبُوْا اِلَيْهِ\nWA ARGHABU ILALLAAHI FEEMAA RAGHIBOO ILAYH\nI turn in longing to Allah for that which they longed for from Him.\nوَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللهِ\nWA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAH\nThere is no power and no strength except with Allah.",
    "Bismillah alladhi La Yadurr ×3\nRecite 3 times in the morning and 3 times in the evening:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الَّذِىْ لَا يَضُرُّ مَعَ اِسْمِهٖ شَىْءٌ فِى الْاَرْضِ\nBISMILLAAHIL LADHEE LAA YADURRU MA'AS MIHEE SHAY'UN FIL ARD\nIn the name of Allah, with Whose name nothing in the earth\nوَلَا فِى السَّمَاۤءِ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nWA LAA FIS SAMAA'I WA HUWAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEM\nor in the heaven can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.",
    "Thanksgiving of Prophet Noah (a.s.)\nEvery morning and evening, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اُشْهِدُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE USH-HIDUK\nO Allah, I call You to witness\nاَنَّهٗ مَا اَمْسٰى وَاَصْبَحَ بِىْ مِنْ نِعْمَةٍ\nANNAHOO MAA AMSAA WA ASBAHA BEE MIN NI'MAH\nthat whatever bliss I enjoy in this evening and this morning,\nاَوْ عَافِيَةٍ فِىْ دِيْنٍ اَوْ دُنْيَا\nAW A'AFIYATIN FEE DEENIN AW DUNYAA\nand whatever wellbeing in a religious or worldly affair,\nفَمِنْكَ وَحْدَكَ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَكَ\nFAMINKA WAHDAKA LAA SHAREEKA LAK\nis from You alone, without any partner with You.\nلَكَ الْحَمْدُ وَلَكَ الشُّكْرُ بِهَا عَلَىَّ\nLAKAL HAMDU WA LAKASH SHUKRU BIHAA A'LAYYA\nTo You be all praise and to You be all thanks for it,\nحَتّٰى تَرْضٰى اِلٰهَنَا\nHATTAA TARDAA ILAAHANAA\nuntil You are pleased, O our God.\nOther narrations give this form, recited 10 times every morning and evening:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّهٗ مَا اَصْبَحَ بِىْ مِنْ نِّعْمَةٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAHOO MAA ASBAHA BEE MIN NI'MAH\nO Allah, whatever bliss I enjoy in this morning,\nاَوْ عَافِيَةٍ فِىْ دِيْنٍ اَوْ دُنْيَا\nAW A'AFIYATIN FEE DEENIN AW DUNYAA\nand whatever wellbeing in a religious or worldly affair,\nفَمِنْكَ وَحْدَكَ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَكَ\nFAMINKA WAHDAKA LAA SHAREEKA LAK\nis from You alone, without any partner with You.\nلَكَ الْحَمْدُ وَلَكَ الشُّكْرُ بِهَا عَلَىَّ\nLAKAL HAMDU WA LAKASH SHUKRU BIHAA A'LAYYA\nTo You be all praise and to You be all thanks for it,\nحَتّٰى تَرْضٰى وَبَعْدَ الرِّضَا\nHATTAA TARDAA WA BA'DAR RIDAA\nuntil You are pleased, and after You are pleased.\nEither form is good."
  ],
  "merits": "The traditions about the merits of doing acts of worship at the two hours of daybreak and sunset are too many to be counted. Likewise, too many are the litanies and supplicatory prayers that have been reported from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and his Household (a.s.) to be said at these two times.\n\nSurahs & Dhikr before Sunrise: Ibn Babawayh has reported through a valid chain of authority that Imam Ali Amir al-Mu’minin (a.s.) said, “He who recites [Surah al-Tawhid](A116), [Surah al-Qadr](A101), and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) before sunrise eleven times, his property will be protected against any feared matter.” He (a.s.) is also reported to have said, “Whoever recites [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) before sunrise will be saved from sinning on that day, even if Satan exerts all efforts to make him commit a sin.” Al-Kulayni has reported that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) mentioned many merits for saying the takbir dhikr in the first hour of morning before sunrise.\n\nTahlil ×10: Al-Kulayni, Ibn Babawayh, Shaykh al-Tusi, and other scholars have reported through valid chains of authority that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said: It is obligatory upon every Muslim to say this litany ten times before sunrise and before sunset every day. Confirming the significance of this litany, some narrations hold that if you miss saying this litany at these times, you may make up for it later on, because, on the word of other narrations, it remits from sins.\n\nTakbir ×100 & Tasbih: Ibn Babawayh and other scholars have reported through many chains of authority that Imam Ali ibn al-Husayn and Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said, “He who repeats the Takbir statement (i.e. Allahu Akbar) one hundred times at sunset will be given the reward of one who has manumitted one hundred slaves.” According to another authentic narration, Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) is reported to have said: He who repeats the Takbir statement one hundred times before sunrise and one hundred times before sunset, Almighty Allah will record for him the reward of one who has manumitted one hundred slaves; and he who repeats “Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi” ten times will be granted by Allah ten rewards. If he repeats it more, he will be granted more rewards.\n\nAl-Tusi, may Allah have mercy upon him, and Ibn Tawus report the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) as saying: Whoever says “Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi, subhan Allahi al-’Azim” one time in the morning and one time in the evening, Almighty Allah sends an angel to Paradise with a silver shovel. The angel then gathers some clay of Paradise, which is sweet smelling musk, fixes a plant, surrounds it with a fence, places a door on it, and writes on the door that this plant is for so-and-so (i.e. writes the name of that person on the door). In another validly reported tradition, Sayyid Ibn Tawus reports Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) to have said that whoever says this doxology intending to glorify Almighty Allah but not to express amazement, Almighty Allah will erase one thousand of his sins, record for him one thousand rewards, decide for him one thousand rights of intercession, raise him one thousand ranks, and creates from these words a white bird uttering these words of glorification continuously up to the Resurrection day and the reward of the bird’s glorification words will be recorded for that person.\n\nTasbihat al-Arba’a ×10: Through a valid chain of authority, Ibn Babawayh reports Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) to have quoted the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) as saying: In Paradise, there are chambers whose inside can be seen from their outside and whose outside can be seen from their inside. These chambers are dwelled by some of my people who speak good wording, serve food (generously), exchange greetings, and pray at night when the others are asleep. To speak good wording means to repeat this doxology ten times every morning and evening.\n\nIn the book of al-Mahasin, al-Barqi has reported through an authentic chain of authority that Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) related that one day the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) passed by a man who was sowing a plant in his orchard. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) stopped and said to him, “May I lead you to a thing that is firmer in sowing, quicker in yielding, and sweeter in fruit?” “Yes,” the man answered, “You may, Allah’s Messenger.” The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) instructed him to say this every morning and evening: “If you do, for each statement you will be given trees in Paradise from various kinds of fruits. These statements are the ever-abiding, good deeds about which Almighty Allah has said in His Book that they are best and more enduring than the wealth of this world.”\n\nVerses of Glorification ×3: Ibn Babawayh has reported though a valid chain of authority that Imam Ali (a.s.) said: Whoever repeats these verses three times before or after evening, will not miss any good item on that day, and will be saved from all evils. The same reward will be for one who repeats them in the morning.\n\nLa Hawla & Relief from Poverty: In the book of al-Mahasin, al-Barqi has reported through an authenticated chain of authority that Imam al-Rida (a.s.) said: Whoever repeats this litany three times in the morning and in the evening must not fear any devil, despotic ruler, leprosy, or mycobacterium. As for me, I repeat it one hundred times. The same litany is also recited seven times after the dawn (fajr) and the Evening Prayers.\n\nThrough a valid chain of authority, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have related that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) had missed one of Ansar (people of al-Madinah who gave shelter and supported the Holy Prophet and the earlier Muslims). When the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) met him afterwards, he asked, “What kept you away from us?” The man answered, “It was poverty and long disease, Allah’s Messenger.” The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said, “May I teach you some words that remove poverty and disease away from you?” “Yes,” the man answered, “You may, Allah’s Messenger.” The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) then taught him [Dua for Relief from Poverty & Ailments](E54), to be said in mornings and evenings.\n\nIsti’adha ×10: In many validly reported traditions, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: Repeat this guard-seeking prayer ten times before sunrise and before sunset.\n\nDua Muqallib al-Qulub ×3: In the book of Falah al-Sa’il, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: What prevents you from saying this supplicatory prayer three times every morning and three times every evening?\n\nMorning Praise: Al-Qutb al-Rawandi has reported that Imam Ali Amir al-Mu’minin (a.s.) quoted the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) as saying: He who begins his day without mentioning these four graces, I fear lest he will lose the bliss he is enjoying. In the book of al-Balad al-Amin, it is reported that Salman the Persian, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Any servant who repeats this doxology three times in the morning, Almighty Allah will most surely fend off seventy kinds of afflictions, the easiest of which is distress, from him.\n\nDua Asbahtu Billahi Mu’minan: Through a valid chain of authority, al-Kulayni reports Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) to have said: In the morning, you may say this litany.\n\nBismillah alladhi La Yadurr ×3: In the book of al-Balad al-Amin, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: No tribulation will afflict one who repeats this litany three times in the morning until evening, and no tribulation will afflict him who repeats it three times in the evening until the next morning.\n\nThanksgiving of Prophet Noah (a.s.): Al-Kulayni, Ibn Babawayh, and other scholars have reported through authenticated and valid chains of authority that Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) says: Prophet Noah (a.s.) was described as most grateful servant (indication of Qur’an, 17:3), because he used to say this doxology every morning and evening. According to other narrations, Prophet Noah (a.s.) used to repeat the second form ten times every morning and evening."
